<section id="A1.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.1 </span>Inter-Trait Rank Shifts</h5>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As per the context variation analysis, we performed a series of paired Wilcoxon signed-rank tests on the consistent pairwise decisions for each country-country pair within each trait, reporting the matched rank-biserial effect size <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{rb}=(\mathrm{wins}_{A}-\mathrm{wins}_{B})/(\mathrm{wins}_{A}+\mathrm{wins}_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>wins</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>wins</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>wins</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>wins</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{rb}=(\mathrm{wins}_{A}-\mathrm{wins}_{B})/(\mathrm{wins}_{A}+\mathrm{wins}_{B})</annotation></semantics></math> and the two-sided normal-approximation <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value (matching the <span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jaspTTests::TTestPairedSamples(wilcoxon=TRUE, effectSize=TRUE)</span> default). Cells with a theoretical <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|r_{rb}|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|r_{rb}|=1</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. one country wins every consistent decision) carry a <sup id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">p</sup> superscript to denote a perfect separation. Cell value <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math> row vs. column; positive (greener/bluer) means the row country is preferred for that trait. Sig. markers: <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}^{*}{=}p{&lt;}.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{*}{=}p{&lt;}.05</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}^{**}{=}p{&lt;}.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{**}{=}p{&lt;}.01</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}^{***}{=}p{&lt;}.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{***}{=}p{&lt;}.001</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">n.s.</span> non-sig. The results organised by <span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">trait</span> are as follows:</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.2 </span>Llama-3.1-8B – Trait Variation</h5>

